A per-page map of the chunks translated code occupies, so a data write to
a page with code at both ends stops walking its whole TB list (patch 15's
early-out, made fine-grained).

Patch 15 gave every PageDesc the byte range [code_lo, code_hi] its TBs
cover, and a guest write outside it returned before any walk. That is
right for a page with one stale TB, and wrong for the page a Win9x module
is made of: code at both ends, data between, so every data write lands
inside the range and pays PAGE_FOR_EACH_TB over the page's entire list --
twice since patch 24, whose soft-immediate check is asked first and walks
the same list. 3DMark 99 on Win98 spent 57 % of QEMU in the two walks
(`soft_imm_absorbs__locked` 29 %, `tb_invalidate_phys_page_range__locked`
28 %) during its CPU and fill-rate tests, and invalidated nothing.

The range becomes a uint64_t: one bit per 1/64 of the page (64 bytes of a
4 KiB one), set in tb_page_add for every chunk a TB touches and restarted
when the first TB lands on an empty page, exactly the lifetime the range
had. It is a superset of what the list covers at every moment (bits are
never cleared while a TB remains), so a write whose chunks carry no bit
cannot hit a block, and tb_invalidate_phys_range_fast returns at once --
before the soft-immediate walk as well, which can only have found nothing
there. A self-modifying loop writes inside its own chunks and is handled
exactly as before.

It is patch 15's cut, so it is behind patch 15's switch
(`-accel tcg,tb-invalidate-fast=off`), and with the switch off patch 24 is
asked exactly as it was (patch 29's rule: a switch turns off its own patch
and no one else's).

Measured on 3DMark 99 Max, claude98 (Win98 SE, DirectX 9.0c, our display
driver, 800x600x16, TCG, pentium3), the user's own settings: 3334 3DMarks
-> 5894 (CPU 3DMarks 10969 -> 11648). The walks fall from 57 % of QEMU to
0.1-0.4 % in every 20 s of the run. The race test goes from 25 fps to the
60 Hz flip cap, the first-person test from 4.5 to 13.6 fps.

Test: tools/smc-guest-test.py (every case in all four soft-imm x
smc-same-value combinations, the soft-imm path required to absorb), the
DOS batteries, and the 3DMark 99 score on claude98 (doc 19).

